  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You magically transport yourself, reappearing amid a burst of moonlight. As a Bonus Action, you teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see, and you have Advantage on the next attack roll you make before the end of this turn.</p><p>You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. You can also regain uses by expending a level 2+ spell slot for each use you want to restore (no action required).</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-fQNfNPvTSXWuXepa\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>This feature includes an activity with an Active Effect for tracking when you have Advantage but it does not automate the Advantage.</p><p>It also includes a Recharge with Spell Slot activity which can be used to convert spell slots into uses of this feature. You can select higher level slots by increasing the scale.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
